# 14. Risks and Constraints

## Inventory Accuracy

Digital inventory may become inaccurate if product movements are not recorded correctly.

## Incorrect User Input

Employees may accidentally enter incorrect quantities or information.

## Transaction Validation

The application must prevent invalid transactions and prevent inventory quantities from becoming negative.

## Authentication

Only authorized users should have access to protected inventory functionality.

## Database Consistency

Inventory quantities and transaction history must remain synchronized.

## Multiple Users

Several employees may interact with inventory information.

## Usability

The application must make inventory transactions fast and simple enough to use during normal hotel operations.

## Individual Development

The project is being developed by one person, so project scope and development time must be carefully controlled.

## Scope Expansion

Advanced functionality must not delay completion of the core MVP.

